# IIQ AngularJS + Legacy Import & Registration Patterns

## AngularJS Module Registration

**Register directives, services, filters in the module file:**

```javascript
// web/ui/js/common/module.js (shared) or web/ui/js/{feature}/module.js (feature)
angular.module('sailpoint.{module}', [])
    .directive('spDatePicker', spDatePicker)
    .service('DateValidationService', DateValidationService)
    .filter('dateFormat', dateFormat);
```

**Order:** directives → services → factories → filters → controllers → constants

**Never register in the component file itself** — always in the module file.

## JSPM Imports (ES6 style in IIQ)

```javascript
// Relative imports for same-feature files
import DateValidationService from './service/DateValidationService';

// Cross-feature imports use full path from web/ui/js/
import 'common/directive/spDatePicker';
import 'common/service/DateValidationService';

// Third-party (from JSPM packages)
import angular from 'angular';
import 'angular-ui-router';
```

**Import order:** third-party → `common/` → feature/ → relative

## ExtJS Component Registration

```javascript
Ext.define('SailPoint.grid.MetadataGrid', {
    extend: 'SailPoint.grid.AbstractGrid',
    requires: [
        'SailPoint.store.MetadataStore',
        'SailPoint.model.MetadataModel'
    ],
    // ...
});
```

## XHTML Namespace Declarations

```xml
<ui:composition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"
    xmlns:ui="http://java.sun.com/jsf/facelets"
    xmlns:h="http://java.sun.com/jsf/html"
    xmlns:f="http://java.sun.com/jsf/core">
```

Only declare namespaces you actually use in the file.
